  "id": "628932",
  "subject": [],
  "title": "Argaeus (mountain)",
  "provenance": "Barrington Atlas: BAtlas 64 A3 Argaeus M.",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/mountain"
  ],
  "details": "<p>Argaeus Mons is commonly depicted on coins from <a class=\"internal-link\" href=\"../628949\" title=\"Cappadocia\">Cappadocia</a>. <a class=\"internal-link\" href=\"../629035\" title=\"Mazaka/Eusebeia/Caesarea\">Casearea</a>, just north of the mountain, hosted a mint.</p>\r\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"http://numismatics.org/collectionimages/19501999/1983/1983.159.38.rev.width350.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>The reverse side of the <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://numismatics.org/collection/1983.159.38\">coin (1983.159.38)</a> depicted in the image above, used by permission of the American Numismatic Society, bears a representation of Argaeus Mons.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Erciyes Da\u011f\u0131 in Turkish. A massive volcanic mountain, the highest peak of the Antitaurus range. Commonly depicted on coins from Cappadocia.",
